# Code commenter after implementation

After **behavioral** implementation is done on a feature branch (logic in place; tests and [test-gap pass](testing-gap-after-implement.mdc) done per [testing-discipline.mdc](testing-discipline.mdc)), run a **comment pass** before opening a draft PR or ending the implementation handoff.

## Required step

1. Scope: translation units touched by the branch diff vs `main`, or paths the user named.
2. Delegate to the **code-commenter** subagent ([`code-commenter.md`](../agents/code-commenter.md)).
3. Follow [`code-commenter` skill](../skills/code-commenter/SKILL.md) for checklist and summary format if not delegating.
4. **Comment-only** edits in scope; do not change executable behavior in this pass.
5. Commit comment updates on the same feature branch when the pass adds seams, ownership, or transitional notes worth keeping.

## Skip when

- Change is docs-only, tooling-only, or has no edits under `src/` or `include/`
- User explicitly skips a comment pass
- The branch diff vs `main` is unchanged since a code-commenter pass completed this session (re-run after commits that change the diff)

## Workflow order

```text
implement → make test (and related targets) → test-gap pass → code-commenter pass (if src/ or include/ touched) → documentation pass → draft PR
```

See [agent-workflow.mdc](agent-workflow.mdc) for PR and GitHub steps.
